insert('docs/authentication-experience.md','2026-09-11 Account wording, invitation signup and login return — Current','''The public identity entry is always `Sign in / Sign up`, including expired sessions. Received invitations are reachable while signed out; outgoing invitations and contact management remain authenticated. The invitation offers `Create account to accept` and `Already have an account? Sign in`, retains its protected handoff, and returns to explicit acceptance after the chosen hosted flow. The signup route uses Auth0's supported `screen_hint=signup`; no public email-account lookup or account merging is added.

Native session issuance can now include an initial overview after identity and current legal-proof verification. Only after the opaque token is saved and its planner matches does the app publish that overview, without five follow-up requests or an `Opening Rillora` interstitial. A missing initial payload uses the authenticated aggregate `/v1/overview` fallback. Web also loads its core map through this endpoint and defers checks, activity and commerce. Network/provider validation still takes real time; zero latency is not promised. Source, local tests and actual UI are recorded in [this revision](account-matter-ux.md) and its QA; hosted provider settings were not changed.''')
insert('docs/backend.md','Account/matter extension — 2026-09-11','''Migrations0041/0042 add bounded typed `details`, optional Notes and an explicit SQL field allowlist for Details-level recipients. All new matter writes and merged optimistic PATCHes enforce the selected category's minimum locator; the owner-approved maintenance write also checks the resulting required fields. Existing records remain readable and archive/revoke remain possible. Unknown/cross-category detail keys are rejected. Notes and typed details do not enter Name/Directions, public invitation previews, aggregate events or the minimum Start Here export.

The shared record mappers feed authenticated `/v1/overview`; native session exchange can include the same first-screen payload after successful identity/legal/session issuance. This reduces repeated authentication/transaction work without weakening RLS, CSRF, token verification or expiry. Current local suite:136 pass, typecheck/build pass. Existing0040 price migration is included in the pending staging update; no provider prices, entitlements or billing gate change. See [entry contract](account-matter-ux.md) and [QA](../output/qa/rillora-account-matter-ux-20260911/README.md) for the final deployment boundary.''')
insert('docs/interaction-experience.md','2026-09-11 Focused revision — Current','''The latest [account and matter-entry contract](account-matter-ux.md) supersedes the Details / Directions / People tab layout and consumer Profile rehearsal/motivation cards. One continuous native/Web form shows category-specific identity and detail fields, optional directions/people context and Notes at the bottom. Save remains unavailable while a required locator is missing. Switching type keeps the local draft but sends only applicable typed details; long public wallet addresses wrap.

Profile retains actual contacts/sharing, shared reviews, plan access, export, provider instructions, privacy/About and session actions as ordinary rows. Public Profile says `Sign in / Sign up` and offers received-invitation acceptance only. Internal nonoperative rehearsal tests are retained. This focused revision does not replace the public interactive map or claim that every unrelated screen was retested. Current evidence: API136 passes; native132 passes/one existing StoreKit skip; Web57 app-suite passes; new matter/crypto/notes save and reload observed on both clients. Staging and current UI states are tracked in [QA](../output/qa/rillora-account-matter-ux-20260911/README.md).''')
p=root/'docs/interaction-experience.md';s=p.read_text().replace('Status: IMPLEMENTED AND LOCALLY VERIFIED — 2026-09-09','Status: FOCUSED ACCOUNT/MATTER REVISION LOCALLY VERIFIED — 2026-09-11').replace('- Latest evidence: 118 native','- September9 evidence: 118 native');p.write_text(s)
insert('DESIGN.md','Account and matter entry — 2026-09-11','''The Owner replaces the three-part matter editor with one continuous form. Use the [focused contract](docs/account-matter-ux.md): persistent labels and Required/Optional markers, category-specific fields, optional outcome/people context, and Notes last. Native uses a compact adaptive category picker and standard grouped fields; Web uses its existing drawer with the same requirements. Do not restore category-card and three-tab stacks. The palette, typography and reduced-motion/Dynamic Type rules stay in force.

Profile removes Simulation, duplicate role-disclosure rehearsal, preparation motivation and duplicate optional setup. Contacts, shared views/reviews, plan access, export, provider instructions and account/support tasks remain real actions. Fresh and expired public Profile share the `Sign in / Sign up` label and a separate received-invitation entry. A verified login enters its real map directly when the initial payload is available; transient loading uses in-place placeholders, not a branded intermediate page.''')
