p=root/'docs/trusted-sharing.md';s=p.read_text().replace('Status: IMPLEMENTED; SYNTHETIC STAGING DEPLOYED AND CHECKED — 2026-09-10','Status: CORE STAGING CHECKPOINT SEPTEMBER10; SEPTEMBER11 ENTRY/DETAIL EXTENSION LOCALLY VERIFIED').replace('- Saved details: directions plus the existing masked hint, value band, currency and importance fields.','- Saved details: directions plus masked hint, value band, currency, importance, the explicitly allowlisted category-specific details and Notes. Typed details/Notes are absent from Name/Directions and public invitation metadata.');p.write_text(s)
insert('docs/trusted-sharing.md','September11 entry and detail revision','''The signed-out app exposes only the received-invitation entry. Creating a contact, generating a link/QR, changing grants and revoking access use authenticated APIs. New recipients can choose hosted registration, return with the same invitation, then explicitly accept; signup by itself never grants access. The current SQL Details projection enumerates every allowed typed key, so a future private JSON key cannot silently broaden sharing. The B/C, downgrade, unverified/wrong-account and public-metadata cases pass in the current local suite. [Contract](account-matter-ux.md), [QA](../output/qa/rillora-account-matter-ux-20260911/README.md).''')
insert('docs/platform-contract.md','September11 shared entry and matter contract','''Web and native iOS now share category-specific minimum locators and optional Notes, one continuous editor, and exact per-level field projections. Both expose received invitations to guests while requiring authenticated account binding before acceptance; registration preserves that return path. Native renders the overview included with a verified session; Web uses the aggregate core-map endpoint and defers secondary panels. The Profile cleanup removes consumer simulation/motivation clutter without changing nonoperative backend safety controls. Current local checks: API136; native132 pass/one retained StoreKit skip; Web57 app tests. Actual ordinary/large-text UI and deployment evidence are scoped in [QA](../output/qa/rillora-account-matter-ux-20260911/README.md).''')
insert('docs/ios-layout-matrix.md','September11 focused native revision','''Current local Xcode26.6/iOS26.5 Rillora-Matrix-17-Pro checks cover the one-page New/Edit matter form, conditional exchange/on-chain fields, required-save gating, Notes persistence, Profile cleanup and the expired public Profile label. The targeted AX5/Reduce Motion run checks adaptive category/custody pickers and flowing labels/fields. It is not a new five-device or physical VoiceOver matrix. Native132 tests pass with the single pre-existing StoreKit environment skip. [Evidence](../output/qa/rillora-account-matter-ux-20260911/README.md).''')
insert('docs/family-maintenance.md','September11 required matter fields','''Owner approval of a provider/location proposal validates the complete resulting matter against the new [category requirements](account-matter-ux.md). It cannot be used as a second write path around required information. Provider/location proposals stay bounded and explicit; typed details and Notes are not added to the contributor proposal/history contract.''')
insert('docs/solo-operations-and-portability.md','AWS human session troubleshooting — 2026-09-11','''The local operator profile uses `aws login` with the exact IAM identity `rillora-operator`. AWS documents automatic short-credential refresh with an overall session up to12hours. A browser error page alone is not evidence the CLI exchange failed: in this workflow the Owner reported Chrome `ERR_BLOCKED_BY_CLIENT` at127.0.0.1, but the existing CLI completed successfully and STS confirmed the intended identity/account. The unused remote fallback was cancelled; no extra login, permanent key, MFA removal or permission widening was needed.

Before requesting another personal login, inspect the existing command completion and run a bounded STS identity check. If the credential exchange genuinely cannot finish because local callbacks are blocked, use AWS's supported `aws login --remote` and return its authorization code only to that waiting CLI. Never put codes/tokens in chat or project records. Future restricted workload/CI roles reduce routine human-login dependence; they are separate from an indefinitely authenticated human account. [Official behavior and troubleshooting](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/userguide/cli-configure-sign-in.html).''')
